course: dictionary
lesson: 2019
title: A group that joins together
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A confederation is a group of states, countries, organisations or people who join together for a shared purpose. Its members keep much of their own power, so they do not give up everything to become one single thing.
explain: Read the example: «Canada became its own country step by step and peacefully, starting with Confederation in 1867.» The capital C shows a special name for one event. The words «step by step» and «peacefully» are clues: this was a gradual joining, not a war.
explain: Another clue comes from «tied it together from ocean to ocean». Canada was joined up across the land, so a confederation brings separate parts together. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "Canada started with a joining of its provinces in 1867" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: A confederation is a group of states, countries, organisations or people who join together for a shared purpose.
fact: The members of a confederation keep much of their own power.
fact: «Confederation» with a capital C means the joining of Canadian provinces into one country in 1867.
fact: The Swiss Confederation and the Confederate States of the Civil War are both examples of confederations in history.
fact: In sport, football confederations group countries by continent.
exercise: «Canada became its own country step by step and peacefully, starting with Confederation in 1867.» What does Confederation mean here? | A famous king of Canada | A great war between two countries | A railway from ocean to ocean | *The joining of Canadian provinces into one country
exercise: A confederation is a group that joins together. What do its members usually keep? | *Much of their own power | A new king for each member | None of their own power, ever | Only their own sea
exercise: In sport, what do football confederations do? | Build new stadiums for each country | Group players by their age | *Group countries by continent | Choose the referee for each match
test: The Swiss Confederation is an example of what kind of group? | A river that runs through a city | A sports team of one player | *A group of countries joined together for a shared purpose | A single school with many classes
test: Why does the sentence say «step by step and peacefully»? | *The joining happened gradually and without war | The joining happened by accident in one day | The joining was argued over by everyone | The joining was a fast battle
exam: Which sentence uses confederation correctly? | The confederation ran in a race around the park | *The provinces formed a confederation, joining together while keeping much of their own power | A confederation is a loud noise made by a bell | The confederation was a single shop selling bread and cakes
